# The input from which requirements.lock.txt (CPU) and requirements.lock.cu130.txt
# (GPU) are generated. It is NOT installed directly and NOT a lock.
#
# Why it exists (and is not requirements.txt): the backbone is the pinned upstream
# under third_party/franca, imported not copied, so this port's own files import
# only torch, torchvision, numpy and PyYAML (those are requirements.txt). But the
# environment the pinned upstream needs is slightly larger -- franca.hub.utils
# imports tqdm -- and the lock must be a closure over that whole environment.
#
# Regenerate both locks (from the repository root), as for the other methods:
#
#   uv pip compile methods/36_franca/requirements.lock.in \
#       --constraint <a fleet CPU lock's name==version pins, hashes stripped;
#                     torch/torchvision de-+cpu'd> \
#       --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu \
#       --extra-index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
#       --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \
#       --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 \
#       --generate-hashes --no-annotate --no-header
#   # then bin/build-lock.py renders the CPU wheel-comment format; and the cu130
#   # sibling per docs/GPU.md section 2.
torch
torchvision
numpy
PyYAML
tqdm
